### Practical 4: Task Manager RESTful API Test Requests

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Root & Health Check (200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

### 2. Read All Tasks (200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Accept: application/json

### 3. Filter Tasks by Status (?completed=false)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks?completed=false
Accept: application/json

### 4. Read Single Task by ID (200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/1
Accept: application/json

### 5. Create a New Task (201 Created)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Study Express Middleware",
  "description": "Learn logging and error handler pipelines in Node.js",
  "completed": false
}

### 6. Create Task Validation Failure (400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Missing title should cause 400 Bad Request"
}

### 7. Update Task by ID (200 OK)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Set up Node.js & Express Server (Done)",
  "completed": true
}

### 8. Delete Task by ID (200 OK)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/2
Accept: application/json

### 9. Read Non-Existent Task (404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/9999
Accept: application/json

### 10. Test Global Error Handling Middleware (500 Internal Server Error)
GET {{baseUrl}}/error-test
Accept: application/json
